//! Ear-clipping polygon triangulator.
//!
//! A `std`-only port of the `mapbox::earcut` 2.2.x algorithm: build a circular
//! doubly-linked list from the outer ring, splice holes in as bridges, then clip
//! ears one by one. When no ear can be found the algorithm escalates through
//! three fallbacks — filter collinear points, cure local self-intersections,
//! and finally split the ring on a valid diagonal — which is what makes a
//! self-intersecting input such as a spiral triangulable at all.
//!
//! The triangle indices are emitted in exactly the order the reference
//! implementation emits them; the fallback passes are order-sensitive, so the
//! control flow is kept structurally identical rather than idiomatically
//! restructured.

